hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20603","Waki' narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Hasan, Ahmar the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us, he said: We would indeed feel pity for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of how he kept his hands away from his sides when he prostrated. Affan narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, Ahmar the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, he said: We would indeed feel pity for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of how he kept his hands away from his sides when he prostrated."
